# VitalQ hw_v1 board

The electrical source is `hardware/pcb/design.py`. Sheets are written by
`build_sch.py` through `schutil.py`, with explicit millimetre coordinates.
Do not hand-edit the generated `*.kicad_sch` files or `vitalq_hw_v1.kicad_pcb`.

`hardware/pcb/check.sh` regenerates the schematic and the unrouted board, then
runs `kicad-cli` ERC and DRC. ERC must report zero errors. DRC may report
unconnected items, because the board is not routed. Any other DRC error fails
the script. It needs KiCad 9 on the system Python (`pcbnew`), not a virtualenv.

Local symbols and the four local footprints are in `hardware/pcb/lib/` and are
recorded in `lib/SOURCES.md`. `make_lib.py` rebuilds that library, but it needs
an EasyEDA cache at `/tmp/cad/ee` that is not in the repo. CI uses the
committed library.

Wiring that is easy to break:

- ESP32-WROOM-32E-N8R2. GPIO16 stays inside the module. GPIO6–11 are not on the
  symbol. GPIO2 and GPIO12 stay open. GPIO15 is CS_AD5940 and is pulled up.
- The only ADC sense pin is GPIO36 (FSR402 through one 10 kΩ to GND).
- +3V3 comes from the XC6206. +1V8 comes from the TPS7A2018, because AS7341
  VDD is 1.7–2.0 V. PCA9306DCUR is the one extra IC: it translates AS7341 I2C.
- The load sits on VBAT. USB charges the cell and powers the CP2102N. The
  board does not run from USB with the cell missing.
- CP2102N VDD is its own regulator output and is not tied to +3V3.
- PWR_FLAG symbols are schematic-only. They are not in the netlist.

The PCB is a 40 × 62 mm, 4-layer starting placement (widened east to host the
J11/J13 HV-boundary cut-points and clamps). The ESP32 antenna points off the
left edge. Do not put copper in that keep-out. Do not treat the placement as a
finished route.

This board is a research prototype. Do not describe it as a medical device or
claim safety, sterility, or regulatory compliance.
